    56	## Compatibility
    57	
    58	| Component | Supported version |
    59	|---|---|
    60	| Minecraft | 1.18.2 |
    61	| Forge | 40.3.x; compile pin 40.3.0; accepted range `[40.3.0,40.4.0)` |
    62	| Isle of Berk | Exactly 1.2.0; version range `[1.2.0,1.2.0.1)` |
    63	| GeckoLib | 3.0.57; version range `[3.0.57,3.0.58)` |
    64	| Java | 17 |
    65	
    66	The original Isle of Berk JAR and GeckoLib are required dependencies. The companion's common gameplay mixins should be installed with the same companion version on both client and server for multiplayer. Renderer and model mixins load on the client only.
    67	
    68	## Installation
    69	
    70	1. Install Forge 40.3.x for Minecraft 1.18.2. The companion is compiled against 40.3.0 and accepts `[40.3.0,40.4.0)`.
    71	2. Install the original `isleofberk-1.2.0.jar`.
    72	3. Install GeckoLib Forge 3.0.57.
    73	4. For the stable release, put `isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar` in the same `mods` directory. Latest is 1.0.0. Install the same jar on both client and server.
    74	5. Start the game once to generate `config/isleofberkperformance.toml`.
    75	6. For multiplayer, install the same companion version on the client and server.
    76	
    77	The optional `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod remains a separate artifact. Do not merge the JARs or treat this companion as a replacement for it.
    78	
    79	## What is included
    80	
    81	- Configurable AI movement-request throttling for three exact Isle of Berk flight/follow goals.
    82	- Configurable egg hatch-check cadence.
    83	- Configurable ShockEffect particle cadence, while ShockEffect damage cadence remains fixed at 20 ticks.
    84	- Twelve narrow client renderer argument-reuse transformations.
    85	- Eight constructor-constant egg-animation and projectile resource transformations. Dragon geo/anim/texture and egg geo/texture remain uncancelled so Variant Loader can remap them.
    86	- Strict target descriptors and production refmap mappings for the pinned Isle of Berk 1.2.0 bytecode.
    87	
    88	These are narrow companion mixins. The original Isle of Berk behavior remains the source of all non-targeted logic.
    89	
    90	## Configuration
    91	
    92	Forge registers `config/isleofberkperformance.toml` as a COMMON configuration. Comments in the generated file explain the normal/upstream value, the optimized default, and the tradeoff.
    93	
    94	| Key | Optimized default | Upstream/normal value | Effect |
    95	|---|---:|---:|---|
    96	| `ai_move_throttling_enabled` | `true` | `false` | Throttles repeated flight/follow navigation requests. |
    97	| `ai_move_interval_ticks` | `4` | `1` | After a goal starts, the first eligible request runs immediately; later eligible requests use this interval. `1` disables AI cadence throttling. |
    98	| `egg_hatch_check_interval_ticks` | `20` | `20` | The pinned IoB 1.2.0 behavior already checks egg warmth/hatch progress every 20 ticks. Lower values increase work and change timing granularity. |
    99	| `shock_particle_interval_ticks` | `8` | `8` | The pinned IoB 1.2.0 behavior already sends shock particles every 8 ticks. Lower values increase packet/client work and visual density. |
   100	
   101	For the upstream AI cadence baseline, set `ai_move_throttling_enabled = false` or set `ai_move_interval_ticks = 1`. Egg and shock defaults already match the pinned upstream cadence. Changing these values intentionally changes timing or visual behavior.
   102	
   103	## Scope and explicit exclusions
   104	
   105	This release does **not** change:
   106	
   107	- damage cadence, combat rules, target selection, RNG order, or progression semantics;
   108	- the Isle of Berk network protocol or packet format;
   109	- deadlock/safety/chunk-access behavior, including `getChunkNow` and `scratchPosDeadlockFix`;
   110	- Variant Loader compatibility, taming, spawning, or world generation;
   111	- pathfinder algorithms or mutable projectile scratch state;
   112	- shared static particle arrays;
   113	- dynamic model, texture, or layer selection;
   114	- the deferred client packet-handler local-cache optimization.
   115	
   116	The historical Vonix waves through `1.2.1-vonix.13` were audited. The companion intentionally implements only the narrow, defensible subset documented here. See [CANDIDATE-REPORT.md](CANDIDATE-REPORT.md) for the wave-by-wave disposition.
   117	
