README.md:73:4. For the stable release, put `isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar` in the same `mods` directory. Latest is 1.0.0. Install the same jar on both client and server.
README.md:74:5. Start the game once to generate `config/isleofberkperformance.toml`.
README.md:77:The optional `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod remains a separate artifact. Do not merge the JARs or treat this companion as a replacement for it.
README.md:85:- Eight constructor-constant egg-animation and projectile resource transformations. Dragon geo/anim/texture and egg geo/texture remain uncancelled so Variant Loader can remap them.
README.md:92:Forge registers `config/isleofberkperformance.toml` as a COMMON configuration. Comments in the generated file explain the normal/upstream value, the optimized default, and the tradeoff.
README.md:109:- deadlock/safety/chunk-access behavior, including `getChunkNow` and `scratchPosDeadlockFix`;
README.md:110:- Variant Loader compatibility, taming, spawning, or world generation;
README.md:123:- `auditPackagedJar`: companion-only archive; no bundled Isle of Berk or deadlock-fix content
README.md:124:- `configFixture`: required COMMON keys, defaults, and comments present
README.md:126:- Fresh Forge server runtime: all five common gameplay mixins applied; server reached `Done (12.028s)`
README.md:128:- Final artifact SHA-256 matches the uploaded GitHub release asset
README.md:130:No quantitative performance claim is made without matched before/after profiling.
README.md:144:`reobfJar` remains required. The following `canonicalizeReobfJar` task rewrites only ZIP timestamps and timestamp extra fields on that reobfuscated JAR so two clean builds from the same tree are byte-identical. Audit and mapping fixtures inspect that canonical artifact.
