    94	| Key | Optimized default | Upstream/normal value | Effect |
    95	|---|---:|---:|---|
    96	| `ai_move_throttling_enabled` | `true` | `false` | Throttles repeated flight/follow navigation requests. |
    97	| `ai_move_interval_ticks` | `4` | `1` | After a goal starts, the first eligible request runs immediately; later eligible requests use this interval. `1` disables AI cadence throttling. |
    98	| `egg_hatch_check_interval_ticks` | `20` | `20` | The pinned IoB 1.2.0 behavior already checks egg warmth/hatch progress every 20 ticks. Lower values increase work and change timing granularity. |
    99	| `shock_particle_interval_ticks` | `8` | `8` | The pinned IoB 1.2.0 behavior already sends shock particles every 8 ticks. Lower values increase packet/client work and visual density. |
   100	
   101	For the upstream AI cadence baseline, set `ai_move_throttling_enabled = false` or set `ai_move_interval_ticks = 1`. Egg and shock defaults already match the pinned upstream cadence. Changing these values intentionally changes timing or visual behavior.
   102	
   103	## Scope and explicit exclusions
   104	
   105	This release does **not** change:
   106	
   107	- damage cadence, combat rules, target selection, RNG order, or progression semantics;
   108	- the Isle of Berk network protocol or packet format;
   109	- deadlock/safety/chunk-access behavior, including `getChunkNow` and `scratchPosDeadlockFix`;
   110	- Variant Loader compatibility, taming, spawning, or world generation;
   111	- pathfinder algorithms or mutable projectile scratch state;
   112	- shared static particle arrays;
   113	- dynamic model, texture, or layer selection;
   114	- the deferred client packet-handler local-cache optimization.
   115	
   116	The historical Vonix waves through `1.2.1-vonix.13` were audited. The companion intentionally implements only the narrow, defensible subset documented here. See [CANDIDATE-REPORT.md](CANDIDATE-REPORT.md) for the wave-by-wave disposition.
   117	
   118	## Verification
   119	
   120	The 1.0.0 release is the current companion tree, rebuilt after the version promotion. Historical 0.3.0 evidence against the pinned original dependency with Java 17 and Gradle 7.5.1:
   121	
   122	- `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`
   123	- `auditPackagedJar`: companion-only archive; no bundled Isle of Berk or deadlock-fix content
   124	- `configFixture`: required COMMON keys, defaults, and comments present
   125	- `RendererBytecodeFixture`: 12 renderers and 36 fixed-resource methods passed
   126	- Fresh Forge server runtime: all five common gameplay mixins applied; server reached `Done (12.028s)`
   127	- Independent GPT-5.6-SOL review: `PASS`
   128	- Final artifact SHA-256 matches the uploaded GitHub release asset
   129	
   130	No quantitative performance claim is made without matched before/after profiling.
   131	
   132	## Building from source
   133	
   134	Requires JDK 17. The pinned local validation command is:
   135	
   136	```bash
   137	JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-amd64 \
   138	PATH=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-amd64/bin:$PATH \
   139	./gradlew clean check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks
   140	```
   141	
   142	The exact original Isle of Berk dependency is required locally for the bytecode fixture and is intentionally not committed or redistributed.
   143	
   144	`reobfJar` remains required. The following `canonicalizeReobfJar` task rewrites only ZIP timestamps and timestamp extra fields on that reobfuscated JAR so two clean builds from the same tree are byte-identical. Audit and mapping fixtures inspect that canonical artifact.
   145	
   146	## Documentation
   147	
   148	- [Changelog](CHANGELOG.md)
